    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "omg help i just spilled boiling tea on my wrist and hand... its so bad. the skin is turning white and there are these huge blisters forming already. it feels like my skin is literally melting and the air hitting it hurts so much i cant even breathe. should i just slather a bunch of heavy vaseline or maybe some thick cooking oil on it to seal it up so the air doesnt touch the raw parts? it feels like it needs to be covered in something thick to stop the stinging.",
